# An existential of a trait with a method that needs one dictionary for a whole
# collection: `Total: fn [a] -> Nat` takes the trait's type inside an array, and an array
# of hidden values has a dictionary an element (the coordinator's first ruling, 11
# November 2026, on Type System ch. 3, "Existentials": "An existential is the one feature
# that makes an implementation keep a dictionary at run time", one a packed value), none
# when it is empty and several when its elements were packed at different types. So the
# method cannot be asked of `any ^Counted`, and the trait cannot stand behind `any`.
# The code and the wording are a guess. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering branch;
# subject to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

trait ^Counted a:
    Total: fn [a] -> Nat

impl ^Counted Nat:
    fn Total ns = Fold ns, 0, \|acc, n| acc + n

Hide: fn Nat -> any ^Counted
fn Hide n = any n

Doubled: fn a -> Nat where a: ^Counted
fn Doubled x = Total [[x, x]]

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"{Doubled (Hide 3)}")
